    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f83e2f08-d6fe-5b70-8692-0831595df635" activityNameId="7775d416-5c80-5a3b-9fdc-5b37083ca523" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board, through-hole, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board, through-hole, at plant
The functional unit represents 1 m2 of a 2-layer FR-4 PWB, surface finished (mixture of Pb-containing and Pb-free methods), with soldermask, for through-hole mount applications, without mounted components. It is designed to be used in industry electronics and simple ICT applications.; UUID: 814e280d-cc43-3041-b462-fc033cf8ce26
The module represents a 0:100 mixture of the datasets “printed wiring board, through-hole, Pb-containing surface, at plant” and “printed wiring board, through-hole, Pb-free surface, at plant”. It is assumed that after 2023 updates, no lead containing electronics are used in the market.
Location: This module is based on information from European producers that are seen as representative for the global situation.
Technology: See included processes for the various surface finishing techniques.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: $ 18.9315 Billion in 1998 (includes all rigid PWB)
Sampling: Mixture of surface finishing based on assumption
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_814e280d-cc43-3041-b462-fc033cf8ce26.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
